  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual) per the combined Statement of Governmental Fund Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances and Statement of Activities (p2, original report p7, gained in the v7 re-trim). Receipts/disbursements and fund balances (1,332,698 / 1,408,010) from its Total governmental funds column (General + Construction); the reconciling-items and Statement of Activities columns are not used (net position 1,675,657 beginning / 7,528,803 ending; depreciation 675,429 appears only there). Warrants issued 1,172,570 as debt_proceeds. Roll-forward: 1,332,698+7,537,667-8,634,925+1,172,570=1,408,010. Collection fees and delinquent taxes are printed as negative revenue lines and kept so (property tax, review). Placement fees as debt service fees. Previously (old trim had only Schedule 1) receipts/disbursements came from Schedule 1 and its budgetary fund balances 967,166 / 1,009,035 were used as beginning/ending cash; those Schedule 1 lines now sit in detail (budgetary basis, Actual and budget columns, p3; differs from the GAAP statement; bond proceeds (net) actual printed as '---'), and beginning cash is null (no prior-year balance sheet). Read pages 1-3 of 3. Balance sheet from the combined Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds and Statement of Net Position (p1, original report p6, gained in the v8 re-trim), Statement of Net Position column (warrants and bonds split by the printed due dates; accrued interest as accrued liabilities; fund-column deferred revenue and fund balances reconcile to '---' there). ending_cash = Cash on deposit with County Treasurer 311,931 and ending_investments = Investments 702,216 (Total governmental funds column, same as the Statement of Net Position column)."
